# conformance/vectors/EXPECTED — which vector families the cross-language gate REQUIRES.
#
# tools/ci/conformance_crosslang.sh refuses to pass when a family listed here has zero files on
# disk. That is the whole point of the file: "we have no vectors yet" and "our vectors vanished"
# look identical to a directory scan, and only one of them is acceptable. Listing a family is
# the commit-time act that arms the gate for it — permanently, since removing a line is a
# reviewable diff and an empty directory is not.
#
# Git does not track empty directories, so absence of a family directory cannot mean anything.
# This file is the manifest that makes the expectation explicit instead of inferred.
#
# One family per line, from: m1pl redact receipt bundle
# Phasing (13 §1, 12 §3.4): m1pl and redact arrive with C3 (Rust + Go); receipt with C6, which
# is also when Python joins the gate. Add each line in the SAME commit that lands its vectors.
#
# The list was empty at C0 on purpose (no implementation was due). m1pl armed with its
# vectors per 13 §11 row C2 — the seed corpus lands with the frame codec, same change.
m1pl
redact
receipt
